# cheat — this very cheatsheet tool

Modern cheat is a single Go binary (github.com/cheat/cheat). The old Python version needed `sudo pip install cheat` to fix docopt module errors — that era is over.

## View a sheet

```sh
cheat tar
ch tar               # alias: clear + cheat | glow (pretty markdown)
```

## List and search

```sh
cheat -l             # list all sheets (alias: chl)
cheat -s ssh         # search sheet contents (alias: cs)
cheat -t ireaneus -l # list sheets with a tag
```

## Create or edit a sheet

```sh
cheat -e mycommand   # opens in $EDITOR (alias: ce)
```

## Real-world: this setup

```sh
# Config lives here; sheets come from the ireaneus-cheatsheets git repo
cat ~/.config/cheat/conf.yml

# Sheets are a git repo — commit and push edits like any other project
cd ~/Public/ireaneus-cheatsheets && git add -A && git commit -m "update sheet" && git push
```

## Real-world: reinstall on a fresh box

```sh
curl -sSL -o /tmp/cheat.gz https://github.com/cheat/cheat/releases/latest/download/cheat-linux-amd64.gz
gunzip -f /tmp/cheat.gz && chmod +x /tmp/cheat && sudo mv /tmp/cheat /usr/local/bin/cheat
```

| Flag | What it does            |
| ---- | ----------------------- |
| -l   | list sheets             |
| -s   | search contents         |
| -e   | edit/create sheet       |
| -t   | filter by tag           |
| -p   | filter by cheatpath     |
